hey makes an impassioned  speech at the white house following the  deadly school shooting in his hometown  of uvalde texas  19 students and two teachers were shot  and killed on may 24th when an  18 year old gunman opened fire in the  school 17 others were injured the gunman  used an ar-15 style rifle to shoot and  injure his grandmother before making his  way to the school he entered through an  unlocked side door and remained inside  for more than an hour as multiple  students inside the building called  9-1-1 he was later shot and killed by  border patrol agents mcconaughey who was  born in uvalde texas says he visited the  city just one day after the shooting he  says his mother taught kindergarten just  one mile from robb elementary school at  a white house address on tuesday  mcconaughey called for stricter gun  control requirements the actor got  emotional when explaining how one  student's body was identified  you could feel the shock  in the town  you could feel the pain  the denial the disillusion anger blame  sadness loss of lives dreams halted  we saw ministries we saw  first responders counselors cooks  families trying to grieve without it  being on the front page news  we met with the local funeral director  and countless morticians who who hadn't  slept since the massacre the day before  because they've been working 24 7 trying  to handle so many bodies at once  so many little  innocent bodies  who had their entire lives still yet to  live  maite wore  green high top converse  with a heart she had hand drawn on the  right toe because they represented her  love  of nature camilla's got these shoes can  you show these shoes please  wear these every day  green converse with a heart on the right  toe  this is the same green converse  on her feet that turned out to be the  only clear evidence that could identify  her after the shooting  we need to invest in mental health care  we need to save for schools  we need to restrain sensationalized  media coverage  we need to restore our family values  we need to restore  our american values  and  we need responsible gun ownership  responsible gun ownership we need  background checks  we need to raise the minimum age to  purchase an ar-15 rifle  2 21  we need a waiting period for those  rifles we need red flag laws and  consequences for those who abuse them  these are reasonable practical tactical  regulations  meanwhile the department of justice  announced it's launching a critical  review of the law enforcement response  following the deadly shooting in a  release the doj says the review would  work to provide an account of the law  enforcement response identify lessons  learned from that response and work to  outline the best practices for future  first responders involved in similar  incidents since the shooting law  enforcement has faced backlash for its  response time many noting it took  officers one hour and 17 minutes to  break into the school after the gunman  first walked inside the doj now says its  office of communities oriented policing  services will conduct the review  philip where do you think the doj will  start their investigation into the  evolving police response to this mass  shooting  well the good news is it's a critical  review and not a criminal probe the  first thing that they're going to do is  they're going to look at the time of the  call for help  the time of arrival  how many deaths occurred before they  forced entry into that final room where  the gunman was killed  ultimately i think the doj is going to  put this local police department on a  path toward avoiding a receivership so  they know what best practices to use if  god forbid in the future they ever have  another mass murder anywhere be it a  market school anywhere in public  you know it's heartbreaking to think  that we're preparing for the next one  but terry what was your take away from  mcconaughey's speech and what action do  you think is needed next  you know i think mcconaughey was very  passionate he is from vivaldi i'm so  glad he came i'm so glad he spoke up and  i think people are listening to what he  had to say but i don't think it's enough  he talked about mental health care safer  schools restraining the media family  values all of those things are excellent  but at the end of the day he basically  said you know if you have an ar-15 raise  the age and make sure that you are not a  red flag risk but in my humble opinion i  don't think that anyone really needs an  ar-15 you don't need to have an ar-15 if  you're going hunting or even if you're  protecting your home so i do think we  need to start with what he said but i  think we should probably go further now  let's hope they'll make some steps going  forward in this crisis well thank you  for joining us here on law and crime  daily we'll see you next time as we  discuss justice in america  [Music]  you
 

